# Netlify redirects.
#
# Every page here is a .html file served at a clean, slash-less URL by
# Netlify's "Pretty URLs" processing — about.html answers at /about. That is
# how this site has always worked and these URLs are already indexed, so the
# layout keeps it rather than switching to directories, which would make
# Netlify redirect /about to /about/ and change every URL Google knows.
#
# The problem Pretty URLs leaves behind is that the .html form ALSO answers
# 200. The same page on two URLs splits its ranking signals. These rules fold
# the .html form onto the clean one.
#
# The ! is required. Without it a static file that exists wins over a redirect,
# and about.html very much exists. With it, the redirect runs first.
#
# No loop risk: the rule matches the request path /about.html. A request for
# /about never matches it — Pretty URLs serves that from about.html internally
# as a rewrite, not a redirect.

/index.html                              /                                    301!
/about.html                              /about                               301!
/contact.html                            /contact                             301!
/services.html                           /services                            301!
/service-areas.html                      /service-areas                       301!
/privacy.html                            /privacy                             301!
/terms.html                              /terms                               301!
/accessibility.html                      /accessibility                       301!

